S640 Resonance Product-Ledger Atlas
====================================

Thesis
------
The shared object is not a single theorem.  It is a proof-design schema: scalar quotient + retained side channel + residual obstruction.
The failures all happen when the scalar is treated as the object.  Progress happens when the side channel is made first-class.

Atlas
-----
- H=21 impossibility
  scalar: Hamiltonian-path count 21
  side channel: strong-component norm, c3/odd-cycle budget, OCF packet
  status: closed: 7 and 21 are permanent H-gaps in repo ledger
  instrument: finite strong-window closure plus Busch/Moon lower bounds
  barrier: raw H forgets the strong/OCF side conditions
- LRC n=14
  scalar: C=2n-1=27 shell clock
  side channel: gcd strata 1/3/9, unit/nonunit shells, carry/owner data
  status: open in full; Res_27 least-positive quotient classified
  instrument: THM-407 shell fold, Res_27 pinch certificate, carry conservativity
  barrier: least-positive quotient forgets lift/CRT branch ownership
- unit distance n=21
  scalar: 21 vertices, 57 unit edges
  side channel: 20-edge unit spine plus 37=C_hex(3) bulk, traceability, ears
  status: exact stored 57-edge cores traceable; n=22 frontier open
  instrument: Hamiltonian-spine DP and Moser carrier beam
  barrier: raw edge count forgets embedding, direction support, spine/bulk split
- A000568 / self-converse
  scalar: unrooted tournament class count
  side channel: Burnside partitions, fixed/merged/nonfixed, q-deformation, transporters
  status: active method: extend hard sequences by companion shadows
  instrument: Burnside q-shadow and anti-coset transporter quotient
  barrier: raw next term forgets fixed-point and orbit side channels
- Schanuel / pi-e
  scalar: algebraic/rational shadow
  side channel: algebraic independence, trace/norm/discriminant, transverse shadows
  status: conditional completion; S636 proves at least two of S/P/D transcend
  instrument: Vieta carrier, Lindemann-Weierstrass fallout, Schanuel conditional
  barrier: individual transcendence does not control algebraic curves
- twin primes
  scalar: prime gap 2
  side channel: admissible tuple, singular series, sieve weights, parity barrier
  status: open; bounded gaps known, H_1 <= 246 in Polymath8b ledger
  instrument: Maynard-Tao/Polymath sieve weights
  barrier: parity problem: sieve sees almost-primes better than primes
- Goldbach
  scalar: even N as p+q; odd N as p+p+p
  side channel: major/minor arcs, local congruences, singular series, density
  status: weak/ternary proved by Helfgott; strong/binary open
  instrument: circle method plus explicit minor-arc bounds
  barrier: minor arcs and local-to-global transfer are the hard residue side

